---
import { getEntry, render } from "astro:content";
import { Table, TableBody, TableCell, TableHead, TableHeader, TableRow } from "../../components/ui/table";
import DocShell from "../../layouts/DocShell.astro";
import { sdkSidebar } from "../../lib/sdk-nav";
import "../../styles/prose.css";

const snippet = await getEntry("snippets", "python-sdk");
const { Content: Example } = await render(snippet!);
---

<DocShell title="SDKs" description="Client libraries for the OpenHAL hub protocol." sidebar={sdkSidebar()}>
  <p>An SDK handles the hub protocol for you, and the hub's safety kernel still checks every command.</p>
  <Table containerClassName="table-wrap">
      <TableHeader>
        <TableRow><TableHead scope="col">Language</TableHead><TableHead scope="col">Package</TableHead><TableHead scope="col">Status</TableHead></TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
        <TableRow>
          <TableCell><a href="/sdks/python/">Python</a></TableCell>
          <TableCell className="mono">openhal.client</TableCell>
          <TableCell>reference</TableCell>
        </TableRow>
        <TableRow>
          <TableCell><a href="/sdks/typescript/">TypeScript</a></TableCell>
          <TableCell className="mono">not published</TableCell>
          <TableCell><span class="status planned">planned</span></TableCell>
        </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
    </Table>
  <h2 id="python">Python</h2>
  <p>The Python SDK ships in the repository, and a blocked command returns a decision that carries the error code.</p>
  <Example />
  <p><a href="/sdks/python/">Python guide</a> and <a href="/sdks/python/reference/">API reference</a></p>
</DocShell>
